WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
Welcome to Place Value and Estimation.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.820
Large numbers need not mean long calculations.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.300
When you see a number close to a tidy round number,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.720
you can take it apart, work with easier pieces, and put

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.820
it back together exactly.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Let's see an easy, medium, and hard example.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.510
Easy problem. Work out three hundred and ninety-eight plus two

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.620
hundred and seven, without a calculator.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.570
First estimate: four hundred plus two hundred is about six

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.120
hundred. That tells us the size of a sensible answer before

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:30.880
we calculate.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.300
Write three hundred and ninety-eight as four hundred minus

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.100
two. Write two hundred and seven as two hundred plus seven.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.935
Together that is six hundred, plus five, giving six hundred

00:00:42.935 --> 00:00:46.800
and five. Estimation checks the scale; careful adjustment

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.200
gives the exact result.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.650
Medium problem. Find fifty-seven times ninety-eight.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.510
Ninety-eight is close to one hundred, so imagine a rectangle

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.570
fifty-seven units high and one hundred units wide.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.470
Then remove a strip only two units wide.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.290
This picture is an equation waiting to happen.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.990
The large rectangle has area fifty-seven times one hundred,

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.190
which is five thousand seven hundred.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.315
The removed strip has area fifty-seven times two, which is one

00:01:16.315 --> 00:01:16.930
hundred and fourteen.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.230
Subtracting gives five thousand, five hundred and eighty-six.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.630
That is close to our estimate, not a huge mysterious product.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.290
Here is the general habit.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.430
Look for a useful round number.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.230
Replace the awkward part by a tidy quantity plus or minus

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.150
a small adjustment.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.150
Keep that adjustment visible.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.610
The picture, the words and the equation should all describe

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.870
the same relationship.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:46.380
Hard problem. Which is greater: forty-nine thousand, nine

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.450
hundred and ninety-six times fifty thousand and four, or fifty

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.330
thousand squared minus seventeen?

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.170
Do not multiply out these enormous numbers.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:58.710
Look at how far each factor is from fifty thousand.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.820
The factors are fifty thousand minus four and fifty thousand

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.720
plus four. The extra strips cancel, leaving fifty thousand

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.260
squared minus four squared.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.720
So the first expression is fifty thousand squared minus

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.640
sixteen. The second is fifty thousand squared minus seventeen.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.040
Therefore the product is greater by exactly one.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.140
A difference of squares replaces a mountain of arithmetic.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.160
Easy, medium, hard: compensation, an area model, and a hidden

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.400
identity. Each uses the same idea: break a number around a

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.080
convenient value, then account for the small change.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.660
Now it's your turn.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.120
Work through the next lesson problems and explain why each

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.120
adjustment is valid.

